[{"generation_id": "5t9isTMcCuGrdneXxie7", "duration_secs": 24.4, "prompt": "MSNR. Malaysian Support and Resistance. Instead of wide zones, it marks exact levels, drawn from candle opens and closes. There are eight levels to know: Classic A, Classic V, QML, RBS, SBR, OCL, trendlines, and the wick fifty percent. Let's break them down, one by one.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/WUygQNjhIUQsOWjppWmP/5t9isTMcCuGrdneXxie7/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183902Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "3A6JcphkH5DtumYKSivL", "duration_secs": 21.36, "prompt": "Classic A. The A-Level. Price rallies into a peak, pulls back, and comes back up to it, drawing the shape of an A. In MSNR, the level sits where the bullish candle closes and the bearish candle opens, not at the wick. When price returns to the A-Level, treat it as resistance, and look for sells.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/TK7yacU5SYZzFmqCs7HM/3A6JcphkH5DtumYKSivL/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183931Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "DfYUrVcLXLo7dyemofee", "duration_secs": 18.32, "prompt": "Classic V. The V-Level. Price drops into a low, bounces, and comes back down to it, drawing the shape of a V. The level sits where the bearish candle closes and the bullish candle opens. When price returns to the V-Level, treat it as support, and look for buys.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/NIra7sILRVQMI8Ivv497/DfYUrVcLXLo7dyemofee/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183946Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "2Iugm2mDb7TWVLWo2jdM", "duration_secs": 27.36, "prompt": "QM, the Quasimodo, and QML, the Quasimodo Level. For a sell, price makes a high, then a higher high, then breaks below the last low. That break is the market structure shift. The high before the higher high is the QML. When price returns to it, look for sells. For a buy, it's the mirror image: a lower low, a break above the last high, then buy from the QML.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/9532SHLLwLGSuRCMCL9r/2Iugm2mDb7TWVLWo2jdM/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183938Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "4q2cUT1lss9rvzxeook7", "duration_secs": 19.92, "prompt": "RBS. Resistance Becomes Support. Price breaks above a resistance level, then pulls back to retest it from above. The old resistance now holds as support, and that retest is where you look for buys. In a strong trend, you'll see it again and again, each new level stepping price higher.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/6BgudoQP3gNStnabH8SG/4q2cUT1lss9rvzxeook7/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183939Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "1khQVq9pnkeCRGn8zf9i", "duration_secs": 18.56, "prompt": "SBR. Support Becomes Resistance. Price breaks below a support level, then rallies back to retest it from below. The old support now acts as resistance, and that retest is where you look for sells. In a downtrend, each broken support becomes the next level to sell from.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/cZrqMvzfjQIuj102guug/1khQVq9pnkeCRGn8zf9i/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T184018Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "LC7CuqHXqPCJwr2awYrW", "duration_secs": 18.32, "prompt": "OCL. The Open Close Level. Where one candle closes and the next one opens at the same price, draw a line. That's the OCL. It works on bullish candles, and on bearish candles. When price comes back to the OCL, it becomes a key level to trade from.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/tauNtuY4dXQtrGpZONmW/LC7CuqHXqPCJwr2awYrW/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183944Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "XR23b3RxZu39ITWMM1rF", "duration_secs": 18.96, "prompt": "Trendlines. Connect two swing highs, or two swing lows, and extend the line. The third touch is where price reacts: a rejection under a falling line, a bounce above a rising one. When the line breaks, the move can be fast. Combine it with a key level for the strongest setups.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/516dw6XMqPgrwQVEr5xv/XR23b3RxZu39ITWMM1rF/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T184002Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "G8m2qyTNVLwIYeY1QdJP", "duration_secs": 20.72, "prompt": "CE W fifty percent. Consequent Encroachment of the Wick. When a candle sweeps a previous low and leaves a long wick, measure that wick. Its fifty percent level is the consequent encroachment, where price often reacts. Use it on the higher timeframe, the one-hour or four-hour, and mirror it for highs.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/ttBOIhsKGNIsnD88qbcQ/G8m2qyTNVLwIYeY1QdJP/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183951Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "AlgZOiLlL3vDc73jCnVe", "duration_secs": 24.96, "prompt": "MSNR. Malaysian Support and Resistance. Instead of wide zones, it marks exact levels, drawn from candle opens and closes. There are eight levels to know: Classic A, Classic V, QML, RBS, SBR, OCL, trendlines, and the wick fifty percent. Let's break them down, one by one.", "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/xi-backend/database/workspace/91237114c47341cba8fb938583f6264d/content_generation/nkCs4EII3F64HfN97uwA/AlgZOiLlL3vDc73jCnVe/content.mp3?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256&X-Goog-Credential=xi-backend-prod%40xi-labs.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20261029%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request&X-Goog-Date=20261029T183903Z&X-Goog-Expires=7200&X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host&X-Goog-"}, {"generation_id": "rslEywMwOqOfR6l1s4al", "duration_secs": 21.52, "prompt": "Classic A. The A-Level. Price rallies into a peak, pulls back, and comes back up to it, drawing the shape of an A. In MSNR, the level sits where the bullish candle closes and the bearish candle opens, not at the wick. Wh